# Everything a RUN produces. The rig writes frame dumps, disassembly listings
# and logs next to its own scripts, which was fine in a temp directory and is
# not fine now that this one is version controlled. 30 MB of screenshots and
# half a megabyte of objdump output are all reproducible from the card image and
# the scripts here, so none of it belongs in git.
#
# THIS RULE ONCE SWALLOWED SOMETHING THAT MATTERED, and the way it did is worth
# keeping in view: `games/godzilla_pro/playfield.png` was the artwork the whole
# artwork half of the virtual playfield depended on, it sat here ignored while
# gameinfo.py's docstring claimed it was checked in, and it was the only
# ignored-but-present file in the rig. Nothing under games/ is generated into
# the checkout any more - mktables.py builds every per-title table and the
# artwork into $PAD_TABLES (under the rootfs, see padpath.py) - so the rule is
# now true rather than merely unnoticed.
*.png

# Derived per-title tables, if anyone points PAD_TABLES back in here.
games/
*.dis
*.log
*.raw
shots/
